// Archetype A (FOUNDATION_PLAN.md): a multi-admiral PvP SKIRMISH universe.
// `Mode: skirmish` makes the player sides (TSN, Orion) mutually hostile, runs the
// Admiral economy at a brisk pace, and ends the match on the LAST SIDE STANDING -
// a side is out when it holds no Headquarters. Needs 2+ player ships (the mission's
// PLAYER_LIST puts player two on Orion). Selectable from the Universe dropdown.

# The Broken Accord
---
Display: Skirmish - The Broken Accord
---
Two fleets, one field of worldlets, and a truce that lasted exactly as long as the
ore did. Build an economy, raise a navy, and end the other admiral's war - the last
side with a Headquarters keeps the Reach.

## Scenario
---
Mode: skirmish
---
Multi-admiral PvP. Set Player Ships to 2 or more - player two flies for Orion.
Victory is the last side standing (raze every enemy Headquarters); a well-placed
strike on the enemy's first HQ - its capital - ends it faster.

## Worldlets

The resource bodies both admirals fight over - build Extractors on them, refine and
bank the yield, spend it on platforms and fleets. A dry worldlet stops producing.

### Cinder World (cinder)
---
Yields: ore 8
Reserve: 4000
Palette: base #8c2f1c, emissive #48180c, clouds #776655
---
A cracked, mineral-rich ember of a world. Miners love it; nobody else does.

### Veiled Giant (veiled_giant)
---
Yields: gas 10
Reserve: 6000
Palette: base #2c4a8c, clouds #b8c4e0, bands 3.7
---
A banded gas giant, its high winds rich in fuel-grade volatiles.

### Haven World (haven)
---
Yields: crew 2, ore 2, gas 2
Reserve: unlimited
Palette: base #2f6e3a, clouds #ffffff
---
A small settled world. People, modest industry, and somewhere to hold.

## Admiralty
---
Worldlet chance: 70%
---
A resource-rich arena (worldlets in most systems) so the fight is over ground worth
holding, not over finding any at all. Economy pace comes from `Mode: skirmish`
(brisk); override it here with `Economy pace:` if you want a slower or faster match.
